      "index": 0,
      "text": "# Railway Dashboard",
      "embeds": [],
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "text": "Railway inland transport is one of the smartest ways to move cargo across a continent.\n\nFreight trains can replace dozens of trucks in a single movement, offering lower CO₂ emissions, reduced noise and far less congestion on roads. Along major European rail corridors, inland rail provides high capacity, reliable transit times and competitive costs, especially when integrated with ports, terminals and last-mile road transport in truly multimodal supply chains.\n\nFor students, understanding inland rail transport means learning how to design efficient and sustainable logistics solutions, where choices about routes, terminals, train types and intermodal connections directly impact cost, lead time and environmental performance of international trade operations.\n\nCLICK HERE",
